therock (The HIP Environment and ROCm Kit) for Slackware-current

This builds AMD's ROCm platform for Slackware-current via TheRock,
AMD's open source build and release system for HIP and ROCm. Since
ROCm 7.14, ROCm is built and released through TheRock; this script
wraps that build into a proper Slackware package installing under
/opt/rocm.

The result is similar in spirit to the excellent ROCm-for-Slackware
scripts by Condor.

Let's be blunt: building ROCm from source is a massive undertaking.
We're talking hours to days of compile time depending on your hardware,
and the disk requirements are genuinely punishing.

Source Cache = 97.6 GiB
Ccache = 3.0 GiB
Build tree (peak) = ~120–150 GiB total
Installed payload (/opt/rocm) = ~25–30 GiB

CPU : Throttle your parallelism. On a 7800X3D we reduced JOBS
      from the default 8 to 4–6 to avoid memory exhaustion

RAM : 32 GB physical minimum. I used 32 GB zram swap just to
      get through the build without OOM kills

Disk : Reserve at least 200 GB in /var/cache and build locations

Time : Set aside a full day or weekend. Don't start Friday evening
       unless you enjoy watching ninja crawl at 3 AM


IMPORTANT: THIS SCRIPT REQUIRES NETWORK ACCESS WHILE RUNNING.
TheRock downloads component sources, toolchains, and dependency
archives from the internet at build time. This script is NOT
suitable for air-gapped or restricted machines. Sources are cached
persistently in $SRC_CACHE (default ~/.cache/therock-src) so
subsequent builds and version bumps fetch only deltas.
Think on how you feel about this before running.

REQUIREMENTS
  git-lfs is a HARD REQUIREMENT (available on SBo).
  After installing git-lfs, run 'git lfs install' once as the user
  running the build (one-time global git config setup).

USAGE
  Default build targets gfx120X-all (RDNA4: gfx1200 + gfx1201),
  covering the RX 9060 / 9070 series and Radeon AI PRO R9700.
  To target an exact architecture only:

    GPU_FAMILIES=gfx1201 ./therock.SlackBuild   (9070 / 9070 XT)
    GPU_FAMILIES=gfx1200 ./therock.SlackBuild   (9060 / 9060 XT)

  Multiple families are semicolon-separated and quoted:

    GPU_FAMILIES="gfx103X-dgpu;gfx110X-all" ./therock.SlackBuild

  See https://rocm.docs.amd.com/en/latest/reference/gpu-specs.html

OPTIONAL BUILD ACCELERATION
  Rebuilds and version bumps benefit from ccache:

    USE_CCACHE=yes ./therock.SlackBuild

  Requires ccache from SBo. The cache persists alongside the source
  cache. Note: first builds are cache-cold; benefits appear from
  the second build onward.

RUNTIME PERMISSIONS
  On stock Slackware-current, /dev/kfd and /dev/dri/renderD* are
  created world read/write (0666), so no group membership is
  required for GPU compute access. If your system tightens these,
  see README.SBo.

See README.SBo for extended instructions, permissions detail, and
troubleshooting.
